        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: Arctic fox, Fjällräven\n- Places: Arctic, circumpolar region\n- Peoples: Circumpolar peoples\n- Concepts: Seasonal camouflage, ancestry, extinction\n\nFacts:\n- The Arctic fox is white in winter and brown in summer.\n- The Arctic fox lives throughout the circumpolar region.\n- The Swedish name for the Arctic fox is Fjällräven.\n- The Arctic fox can trace its roots to an extinct animal that lived in the Arctic.\n- Circumpolar peoples originate from the circumpolar region.",
