        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aba7be60-1033-53c0-98ba-5b956b97f584",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Vulpes qiuzhudingi, Arctic fox, Vulpes lagopus\n- Concepts: Out of Tibet theory, Arctic tundra biome\n- Places: Himalayas, Tibetan Plateau, Arctic, Northern Hemisphere\n- Companies: Fjällräven\n- People: Åke Nordin\n- Groups: Circumpolar peoples, Arctic peoples\n\nFacts:\n- Vulpes qiuzhudingi is an extinct species of fox found in the Himalayas.\n- Vulpes qiuzhudingi is believed to be the ancestor of Vulpes lagopus, the modern Arctic fox.\n- The proposed ancestry from Vulpes qiuzhudingi to Vulpes lagopus supports the Out of Tibet theory that some current arctic species trace their ancestry to species from the Tibetan Plateau.\n- The Arctic fox, also called Vulpes lagopus, white fox, polar fox, or snow fox, is a small fox native to the Arctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere and is common throughout the Arctic tundra biome.\n- The Arctic fox has deep thick fur that is brown in summer and white in winter.\n- Fjällräven, whose name is Swedish for Arctic fox, is a Swedish company specializing in outdoor equipment, mostly clothing and rucksacks.\n- Åke Nordin founded Fjällräven in 1960.\n- Circumpolar peoples and Arctic peoples are umbrella terms for the various indigenous peoples of the Arctic.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d24c3ab3-0729-5411-b028-4a204e99c5c1",
        "text": "Page: Vulpes qiuzhudingi. Sentence: Vulpes qiuzhudingi is an extinct species of fox found in the Himalayas.\nPage: Vulpes qiuzhudingi. Sentence: The species is believed to be the ancestor of \"Vulpes lagopus\", the modern Arctic fox, which would support the \"Out of Tibet\" theory: namely, that a number of current arctic species trace their ancestry to species originally from the Tibetan Plateau.\nPage: Arctic fox. Sentence: The Arctic fox (\"Vulpes lagopus\"), also known as the white fox, polar fox, or snow fox, is a small fox native to the Arctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere and common throughout the Arctic tundra biome.\nPage: Arctic fox. Sentence: It has a deep thick fur which is brown in summer and white in winter.\nPage: Fjällräven. Sentence: Fjällräven (] , Swedish for Arctic fox) is a Swedish company specialising in outdoor equipment—mostly clothing and rucksacks. Fjällräven was founded in 1960 by Åke Nordin (1936–2013).\nPage: Circumpolar peoples. Sentence: Circumpolar peoples and Arctic peoples are umbrella terms for the various indigenous peoples of the Arctic.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
